        <name>fixupAstSymbolTablesToSupportAliasedSymbols</name>
        <param>
          <type>SgNode *</type>
          <declname>node</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Fixup C++ symbol tables to use aliasing symbols for using declarations. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>C++ using declarations and use directives shold have an effect on the symbol table for each scope that will cause a new symbol to be added to support the visability. However within this design the the symbol should be an alias to the original symbol in the original scope.</para><para>This analysis is required only for C++ support, and is similar to work that is currently supporting &quot;use&quot; declarations in <ref refid="namespaceFortran" kindref="compound">Fortran</ref> 90. </para>        </detaileddescription>
